      {
        "link": "https://world.digimoncard.com/rule/?card_no=BT9-012#qaResult_card",
        "num": 1,
        "text": "Official English Q&A for BT9-012 (Mar. 28, 2024)"
      }
    ],
    "rulings": [
      {
        "answer": "No. This effect requires you to trash two cards in this Digimon’s digivolution cards that are the same level as each other. The level of this Digimon doesn't matter.  For example, if there are two level 5 cards in this Digimon’s digivolution cards, you can trash both to prevent this Digimon from being deleted or returned to your hand or deck.",
        "question": "This card’s inherited effect reads, “you may trash 2 cards of the same level”. Does this mean I have to trash 2 cards that are the same level as this card?",
        "reference": "[1]"
      },
      {
        "answer": "Yes, you can.",
        "question": "This card’s inherited effect reads, “you may trash 2 cards of the same level”. If this card is in this Digimon’s digivolution cards, can I include it as one of the trashed cards?",
        "reference": "[1]"
      },
      {
        "answer": "No. When a Digimon is deleted after its DP is reduced to zero, it's considered to be deleted by the game rules, not an effect. This card’s effect only activates when the card is deleted by an effect, so it won't activate in this instance.",
        "question": "An opponent’s effect reduced this Digimon’s DP to zero, deleting it. Does this card’s inherited effect activate?",
        "reference": "[1]"
      }
